{"title": "Sectional Mock #60 (Mixed)", "duration_min": 30.0, "questions": [{"q_en": "<p>The length of a cuboid is 4 cm. If the breadth of the cuboid is four times of its length and height of the cuboid is twice of its length, then what is the lateral surface area of the cuboid?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2328;&#2344;&#2366;&#2349; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; 4 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2328;&#2344;&#2366;&#2349; &#2325;&#2368; &#2330;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366;&#2312; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2368; &#2330;&#2366;&#2352; &#2327;&#2369;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2328;&#2344;&#2366;&#2349; &#2325;&#2368; &#2314;&#2306;&#2330;&#2366;&#2312; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2379;&#2327;&#2369;&#2344;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2328;&#2344;&#2366;&#2349; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2381;&#2357; &#2346;&#2371;&#2359;&#2381;&#2336;&#2368;&#2351; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["380 cm<sup>2</sup>", "440 cm<sup>2</sup>", "260 cm<sup>2</sup>", "320 cm<sup>2</sup>"], "options_hi": ["380 cm<sup>2</sup>", "440 cm<sup>2</sup>", "260 cm<sup>2</sup>", "320 cm<sup>2</sup>"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Length of cuboid = 4 cm</p><p>Breadth of cuboid = 4 * 4 = 16 cm</p><p>Height of cuboid = 4 * 2 = 8 cm</p><p>Lateral surface area of the cuboid = 2(lh + bh)</p><p>= 2 * (4 * 8 + 16 * 8)</p><p>= 320 cm<sup>2</sup></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Length of cuboid = 4 cm</p><p>Breadth of cuboid = 4 * 4 = 16 cm</p><p>Height of cuboid = 4 * 2 = 8 cm</p><p>Lateral surface area of the cuboid = 2(lh + bh)</p><p>= 2 * (4 * 8 + 16 * 8)</p><p>= 320 cm<sup>2</sup></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (3D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>A, B and C run simultaneously, starting from a point, around a circular track of length 1200m, at respective speeds of 2m/s, 4m/s and 6m/s. A and B run in the same direction, while C runs in the opposite direction to the other two. After how much time will they meet for the first time?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>A, B &#2324;&#2352; C &#2319;&#2325; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; &#2360;&#2375; &#2358;&#2369;&#2352;&#2370; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2369;&#2319; 1200 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2366;&#2325;&#2352; &#2335;&#2381;&#2352;&#2376;&#2325; &#2325;&#2375; &#2311;&#2352;&#2381;&#2342; &#2327;&#2367;&#2352;&#2381;&#2342; 2 m/s, 4 m/s &#2324;&#2352; 6 m/s &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2348;&#2306;&#2343;&#2367;&#2340; &#2330;&#2366;&#2354; &#2360;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2342;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; A &#2324;&#2352; B &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2342;&#2367;&#2358;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2342;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2332;&#2348;&#2325;&#2367; C &#2309;&#2344;&#2381;&#2351; &#2342;&#2379; &#2325;&#2368; &#2357;&#2367;&#2346;&#2352;&#2368;&#2340; &#2342;&#2367;&#2358;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2342;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2357;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; &#2346;&#2361;&#2354;&#2368; &#2348;&#2366;&#2352; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2375;&#2306;&#2327;&#2375;?</p>", "options_en": ["10 minutes", "9 minutes", "12 minutes", "11 minutes"], "options_hi": ["10 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335;", "9 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335;", "12 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335;", "11 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335;"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Time taken by A to complete one round = 1200/2 = 600 sec</p><p>Time taken by B to complete one round = 1200/4 = 300 sec</p><p>Time taken by C to complete one round = 1200/6 = 200 sec</p><p>Time at which they will for the 1<sup>st</sup> time = LCM of 600, 300, and 200 = 600 sec</p><p>Hence, they will meet for the first after travelling for 600 sec or 10 min.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Time taken by A to complete one round = 1200/2 = 600 sec</p><p>Time taken by B to complete one round = 1200/4 = 300 sec</p><p>Time taken by C to complete one round = 1200/6 = 200 sec</p><p>Time at which they will for the 1<sup>st</sup> time = LCM of 600, 300, and 200 = 600 sec</p><p>Hence, they will meet for the first after travelling for 600 sec or 10 min.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>Pipe P, pipe Q and pipe R can fill a tank in 18 minutes, 54 minutes and 72 minutes respectively. Pipe P and pipe Q both are opened for 9 minutes. Find the time taken by pipe R alone to fill the remaining tank.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346; P, &#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346; Q &#2324;&#2352; &#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346; R &#2319;&#2325; &#2335;&#2376;&#2306;&#2325; &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 18 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335;, 54 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335; &#2324;&#2352; 72 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2349;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346; P &#2324;&#2352; &#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346; Q &#2342;&#2379;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379; 9 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2326;&#2379;&#2354;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2358;&#2375;&#2359; &#2335;&#2376;&#2306;&#2325; &#2325;&#2379; &#2349;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2309;&#2325;&#2375;&#2354;&#2375; &#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346; R &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2354;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2351;&#2375;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["27 minutes", "26 minutes", "25 minutes", "24 minutes"], "options_hi": ["27 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335;", "26 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335;", "25 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335;", "24 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335;"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Capacity of tank = LCM of 18, 54 and 72 = 216 unit</p><p>Efficiency of pipe P = 216/18 = 12 unit</p><p>Efficiency of pipe Q = 216/54 = 4 unit</p><p>Efficiency of pipe R = 216/72 = 3 unit</p><p>Part of tank got filled in 9 minutes = 9 * (12 + 4) = 144 unit</p><p>Remaining part = 216  -  144 = 72 unit</p><p>Time taken by pipe R alone to fill the remaining tank = 72/3 = 24 minutes</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Capacity of tank = LCM of 18, 54 and 72 = 216 unit</p><p>Efficiency of pipe P = 216/18 = 12 unit</p><p>Efficiency of pipe Q = 216/54 = 4 unit</p><p>Efficiency of pipe R = 216/72 = 3 unit</p><p>Part of tank got filled in 9 minutes = 9 * (12 + 4) = 144 unit</p><p>Remaining part = 216  -  144 = 72 unit</p><p>Time taken by pipe R alone to fill the remaining tank = 72/3 = 24 minutes</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Pipes & Cisterns"}, {"q_en": "<p>If tan(t) = 3/7, where t is an acute angle, then what is the value of cosec(t)?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; tan(t) = 3/7, &#2332;&#2361;&#2366;&#2305; t &#2319;&#2325; &#2344;&#2381;&#2351;&#2370;&#2344; &#2325;&#2379;&#2339; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; cosec(t) &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["&radic;53/7", "&radic;53/3", "&radic;58/3", "&radic;58/7"], "options_hi": ["&radic;53/7", "&radic;53/3", "&radic;58/3", "&radic;58/7"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>tan(t) = 3/7 (Prependicular = 3, base = 7).</p><p>Hypotenuse = &radic;(3&#178; + 7&#178;) = &radic;(9 + 49) = &radic;58</p><p>sin(t) = Prependicular/hypotenuse = 3/&radic;58</p><p>cosec(t) = 1/sin(t) = &radic;58/3</p><p>Option (c) is the correct answer</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>tan(t) = 3/7 (Prependicular = 3, base = 7).</p><p>Hypotenuse = &radic;(3&#178; + 7&#178;) = &radic;(9 + 49) = &radic;58</p><p>sin(t) = Prependicular/hypotenuse = 3/&radic;58</p><p>cosec(t) = 1/sin(t) = &radic;58/3</p><p>Option (c) is the correct answer</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Trigonometry"}, {"q_en": "<p>Let O is the centre of a circle and P is a point outside the circle. If PAB is a secant of the circle which intersects the circle at A and B, and PT is the tangent drawn from P, then find the length of PT. [PA = 3 cm and AB = 9 cm]</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2354;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319; O &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375;&#2306;&#2342;&#2381;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; P &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2361;&#2352; &#2319;&#2325; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; PAB &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2319;&#2325; &#2331;&#2375;&#2342;&#2367;&#2325;&#2366;/&#2360;&#2368;&#2325;&#2375;&#2306;&#2335; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; PAB &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2379; A &#2324;&#2352; B &#2346;&#2352; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2330;&#2381;&#2331;&#2375;&#2342;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; PT, P &#2360;&#2375; &#2326;&#2368;&#2306;&#2330;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2381;&#2346;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358; &#2352;&#2375;&#2326;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; PT &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404; [PA = 3 cm &#2324;&#2352; AB = 9 cm]</p>", "options_en": ["8 cm", "4 cm", "10 cm", "6 cm"], "options_hi": ["8 cm", "4 cm", "10 cm", "6 cm"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p><img width=268 height=192 id=\"Picture 4\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20927/image066.png\"></p><p>Given: PA = 3 cm and AB = 9 cm</p><p>PB = PA + AB = 3 + 9 = 12 cm</p><p>We know that:</p><p>PT<sup>2</sup> = PA * PB</p><p>PT<sup>2</sup> = 3 * 12 = 36</p><p>PT = 6 cm</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=268 height=192 id=\"Picture 4\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20927/image066.png\"></p><p>Given: PA = 3 cm and AB = 9 cm</p><p>PB = PA + AB = 3 + 9 = 12 cm</p><p>We know that:</p><p>PT<sup>2</sup> = PA * PB</p><p>PT<sup>2</sup> = 3 * 12 = 36</p><p>PT = 6 cm</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (2D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>The following pie chart represents percentage wise distribution of total number of students in a class in five different groups.</p><p>Total number of students in the class = 1800</p><p><img width=438 height=336 id=\"Chart 4\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p5292/image004.png\"></p><p>Out of the total number of students in Blue group, respective ratio of boys and girls is 3:2 and out of the total number of students in Green group, respective ratio of boys and girls is 4:3. Number of girls in Blue group is approximately what percent of the number of girls in Green group?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2368;&#2351; &#2310;&#2352;&#2375;&#2326; &#2346;&#2366;&#2306;&#2330; &#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; &#2360;&#2350;&#2370;&#2361;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2319;&#2325; &#2325;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2357;&#2367;&#2342;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352; &#2357;&#2367;&#2340;&#2352;&#2339; &#2325;&#2379; &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;|</p><p>&#2325;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2357;&#2367;&#2342;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; = 1800</p><p><img width=\"438\" height=\"336\" id=\"Chart 4\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p5292/image004.png\"></p><p>&#2344;&#2368;&#2354;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2370;&#2361; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2357;&#2367;&#2342;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375;, &#2354;&#2396;&#2325;&#2375; &#2324;&#2352; &#2354;&#2396;&#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2360;&#2306;&#2348;&#2306;&#2343;&#2367;&#2340; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 3:2 &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2361;&#2352;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2370;&#2361; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2357;&#2367;&#2342;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375;, &#2354;&#2396;&#2325;&#2375; &#2324;&#2352; &#2354;&#2396;&#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2360;&#2306;&#2348;&#2306;&#2343;&#2367;&#2340; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 4:3 &#2361;&#2376;| &#2344;&#2368;&#2354;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2370;&#2361; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2354;&#2396;&#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2352;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2370;&#2361; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2354;&#2396;&#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["87%", "85%", "79%", "83%"], "options_hi": ["87%", "85%", "79%", "83%"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Total number of students in Blue group = 25/100 x 1800</p><p>= 450</p><p>Number of girls in Blue group = 2/5 x 450 = 180</p><p>Total number of students in Green group = 28/100 x 1800</p><p>= 504</p><p>Number of girls in Green group = 3/7 x 504 = 216</p><p>Required percentage = 180/216 x 100</p><p>= 83.33%</p><p>= 83% approx.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Total number of students in Blue group = 25/100 x 1800</p><p>= 450</p><p>Number of girls in Blue group = 2/5 x 450 = 180</p><p>Total number of students in Green group = 28/100 x 1800</p><p>= 504</p><p>Number of girls in Green group = 3/7 x 504 = 216</p><p>Required percentage = 180/216 x 100</p><p>= 83.33%</p><p>= 83% approx.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p>If &#8377;1,875 becomes &#8377;2,625 in 4 years, what will &#8377;24,000 become at the end of 9 years at the same rate of interest, under simple interest?</p>", "q_hi": "&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; 4 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#8377;1,875, &#8377;2,625 &#2361;&#2379; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2360;&#2366;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2339; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327;&#2340; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2342;&#2352; &#2346;&#2352; 9 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#8377;24,000 &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379; &#2332;&#2366;&#2319;&#2327;&#2366;?", "options_en": ["45600", "21600", "4800", "43200"], "options_hi": ["45600", "21600", "4800", "43200"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>We know that S.I =P*R*T/100</p><p>As Rs.1875 becomes 2625 in 4 years,</p><p>So interest = 2625  -  1875 =Rs 750</p><p>So 1875*R*4/100 =750</p><p>R=75000/(1875*4)=10%</p><p>Now for Rs 24000 at the end of 9 years, we get:-</p><p>24000*10*9/100 =Rs 21600</p><p>So Amount = 21600 + 24000= Rs 45600</p><p>Option (a) is the correct answer.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>We know that S.I =P*R*T/100</p><p>As Rs.1875 becomes 2625 in 4 years,</p><p>So interest = 2625  -  1875 =Rs 750</p><p>So 1875*R*4/100 =750</p><p>R=75000/(1875*4)=10%</p><p>Now for Rs 24000 at the end of 9 years, we get:-</p><p>24000*10*9/100 =Rs 21600</p><p>So Amount = 21600 + 24000= Rs 45600</p><p>Option (a) is the correct answer.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simple & Compound Interest"}, {"q_en": "<p>The base area of cylinder is 38.5 cm<sup>2</sup>. Find the curved surface area of the cylinder if its height is 20% more than its radius ? (&#960; = 22/7)</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2348;&#2375;&#2354;&#2344; &#2325;&#2366; &#2310;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; 38.5 cm<sup>2</sup> &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2348;&#2375;&#2354;&#2344; &#2325;&#2368; &#2314;&#2305;&#2330;&#2366;&#2312; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2360;&#2375; 20% &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2348;&#2375;&#2354;&#2344; &#2325;&#2366; &#2357;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352; &#2346;&#2371;&#2359;&#2381;&#2336;&#2368;&#2351; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404; (&#960; = 22/7)</p>", "options_en": ["100 cm<sup>2</sup>", "92.4 cm<sup>2</sup>", "94.2 cm<sup>2</sup>", "85 cm<sup>2</sup>"], "options_hi": ["100 cm<sup>2</sup>", "92.4 cm<sup>2</sup>", "94.2 cm<sup>2</sup>", "85 cm<sup>2</sup>"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Base area of cylinder = &#960;r<sup>2</sup> = 38.5</p><p><img width=97 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p15633/image009.png\"></p><p><img width=143 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p15633/image010.png\"></p><p>r = 3.5 cm</p><p>Height = 120% of 3.5 = 4.2 cm</p><p><img width=379 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p15633/image011.png\"></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Base area of cylinder = &#960;r<sup>2</sup> = 38.5</p><p><img width=97 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p15633/image009.png\"></p><p><img width=143 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p15633/image010.png\"></p><p>r = 3.5 cm</p><p>Height = 120% of 3.5 = 4.2 cm</p><p><img width=379 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p15633/image011.png\"></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (3D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>In the following figure m || n || p. Find the value of B in terms of A.</p><p><img width=336 height=151 id=\"Picture 6\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/91452/image017.jpg\"></p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344; &#2310;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340;&#2367; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; m || n || p &#2361;&#2376;| A &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2344;&#2381;&#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2349; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; B &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;|</p><p><img width=\"336\" height=\"151\" id=\"Picture 6\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/91452/image017.jpg\"></p>", "options_en": ["90 + A", "90 - A", "90 + 2A", "180 - A"], "options_hi": ["90 + A", "90 - A", "90 + 2A", "180 - A"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p><img width=336 height=165 id=\"Picture 7\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/91452/image018.jpg\"></p> <p>In triangle SQU, &#8736;Q = A, &#8736;S = 90. Hence &#8736;SUQ = 90-A</p> <p>&#8736;QUV = 180 - &#8736;SUQ = 90+A (Linear pair)</p> <p>Now, n||p. So &#8736;B = 90+A</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=336 height=165 id=\"Picture 7\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/91452/image018.jpg\"></p> <p>In triangle SQU, &#8736;Q = A, &#8736;S = 90. Hence &#8736;SUQ = 90-A</p> <p>&#8736;QUV = 180 - &#8736;SUQ = 90+A (Linear pair)</p> <p>Now, n||p. So &#8736;B = 90+A</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mixed Practice"}, {"q_en": "<p>One root of the equation mx<sup>2</sup> + 13x  -  63 = 0 is 7/3. The value of m and the other root of equation respectively is - </p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2360;&#2350;&#2368;&#2325;&#2352;&#2339; mx<sup>2</sup> + 13x - 63 = 0 &#2325;&#2366; &#2319;&#2325; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354; 7/3 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; m &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2324;&#2352; &#2360;&#2350;&#2368;&#2325;&#2352;&#2339; &#2325;&#2366; &#2342;&#2370;&#2360;&#2352;&#2366; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; &#2361;&#2376; - </p>", "options_en": ["5, -9/2", "6, 9/2", "5, 9/2", "6, -9/2"], "options_hi": ["5, -9/2", "6, 9/2", "5, 9/2", "6, -9/2"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Since 7/3 is the root of equation mx<sup>2</sup> + 13x  -  63 = 0</p><p>m(7/3)<sup>2</sup> + 13*7/3  -  63 = 0</p><p>49m + 273  -  567 = 0</p><p>m = 294/49</p><p>m = 6</p><p>Now, equation: 6x<sup>2</sup> + 13x  -  63 = 0</p><p>Other root = (-63/6)/(7/3) = -9/2</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Since 7/3 is the root of equation mx<sup>2</sup> + 13x  -  63 = 0</p><p>m(7/3)<sup>2</sup> + 13*7/3  -  63 = 0</p><p>49m + 273  -  567 = 0</p><p>m = 294/49</p><p>m = 6</p><p>Now, equation: 6x<sup>2</sup> + 13x  -  63 = 0</p><p>Other root = (-63/6)/(7/3) = -9/2</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Algebra"}, {"q_en": "<p>In the figure given below, ABCD is a quadrilateral such that AB ll DC and AB produced to E. If &#8736;CBE is 63&#730;, then find the value of 'x'.</p><p><img width=228 height=185 id=\"Picture 3\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p8232/image005.jpg\" ></p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2344;&#2368;&#2330;&#2375; &#2342;&#2367;&#2319; &#2327;&#2319; &#2310;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340;&#2367; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, &#2330;&#2340;&#2369;&#2352;&#2381;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; ABCD &#2311;&#2360; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376; &#2325;&#2367; AB ll DC &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; AB, E &#2340;&#2325; &#2326;&#2368;&#2306;&#2330;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;| &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#8736;CBE 63&#730; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; 'x' &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;|</p><p><img width=\"228\" height=\"185\" id=\"Picture 3\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p8232/image005.jpg\"></p>", "options_en": ["53(2/3)", "71(2/3)", "51(1/3)", "74(1/3)"], "options_hi": ["53(2/3)", "71(2/3)", "51(1/3)", "74(1/3)"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Here, &#8736;ABC + &#8736;CBE = 180</p><p>&#8736;ABC = 180  -  63 = 117&#730;</p><p>In a quadrilateral inscribed in a circle, its opposite angles are supplementary to each other. Then,</p><p>&#8736;ABC + &#8736;D = 180</p><p>117 + 7(y + 1) = 180</p><p>y = 8</p><p>&#8736;A + &#8736;C = 180</p><p>3x + 4y  -  6 = 180</p><p>3x + 4 * 8 = 186</p><p><b>x = 51(1/3)</b></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Here, &#8736;ABC + &#8736;CBE = 180</p><p>&#8736;ABC = 180  -  63 = 117&#730;</p><p>In a quadrilateral inscribed in a circle, its opposite angles are supplementary to each other. Then,</p><p>&#8736;ABC + &#8736;D = 180</p><p>117 + 7(y + 1) = 180</p><p>y = 8</p><p>&#8736;A + &#8736;C = 180</p><p>3x + 4y  -  6 = 180</p><p>3x + 4 * 8 = 186</p><p><b>x = 51(1/3)</b></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (2D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>A shopkeeper has 500 kg sugar. He sold 220 kg sugar at 25% profit and remaining quantity of sugar at p% profit. If overall profit earned by him was 18%, then what is the value of 'p'?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2342;&#2369;&#2325;&#2366;&#2344;&#2342;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2366;&#2360; 500 &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2330;&#2368;&#2344;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2313;&#2360;&#2344;&#2375; 220 &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2330;&#2368;&#2344;&#2368; 25% &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2346;&#2352; &#2324;&#2352; &#2358;&#2375;&#2359; &#2330;&#2368;&#2344;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368; &#2350;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; p% &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2346;&#2352; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2368;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2309;&#2352;&#2381;&#2332;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; 18% &#2341;&#2366;, &#2340;&#2379; 'p' &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["8.5%", "12.5%", "14.5%", "10.5%"], "options_hi": ["8.5%", "12.5%", "14.5%", "10.5%"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Total quantity of sugar = 500 kg</p><p>Quantity of sugar sold at 25% profit = 220 kg</p><p>Quantity of sugar sold at p% profit = 500  -  220 = 280 kg</p><p>Now, by Alligation method:</p><p><img width=379 height=255 id=\"Picture 4\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p8531/image002.png\" ></p><p>Then, (18  -  p): 7 = 220: 280</p><p><b>p = 12.5%</b></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Total quantity of sugar = 500 kg</p><p>Quantity of sugar sold at 25% profit = 220 kg</p><p>Quantity of sugar sold at p% profit = 500  -  220 = 280 kg</p><p>Now, by Alligation method:</p><p><img width=379 height=255 id=\"Picture 4\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p8531/image002.png\" ></p><p>Then, (18  -  p): 7 = 220: 280</p><p><b>p = 12.5%</b></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Ratio & Proportion"}, {"q_en": "<p>Find the sum of all the prime numbers between 70 and 85. </p>", "q_hi": "<p>ab + bc + ca = 14, &#2332;&#2361;&#2366;&#2305; a, b &#2324;&#2352; c &#2358;&#2370;&#2344;&#2381;&#2351; &#2360;&#2375; &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2343;&#2344;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2350;&#2325; &#2349;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339;&#2366;&#2306;&#2325; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; a &gt; b &gt; c, &#2340;&#2379; a &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325;&#2340;&#2350; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["305", "300", "306", "307"], "options_hi": ["3", "2", "4", "5"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Y*Z = 75 = 1 * 3 * 5 * 5</p><p>Pairs of YZ = (1, 75), (3, 25), (5, 15)</p><p>Y  -  Z = 75  -  1 = 74</p><p>Or 25  -  3 = 22</p><p>Or 15  -  5 = 10 </p><p>Hence, option 'b' is correct.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Y*Z = 75 = 1 * 3 * 5 * 5</p><p>Pairs of YZ = (1, 75), (3, 25), (5, 15)</p><p>Y  -  Z = 75  -  1 = 74</p><p>Or 25  -  3 = 22</p><p>Or 15  -  5 = 10 </p><p>Hence, option 'b' is correct.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>What is the H.C.F. of 95, 380, 665?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>95, 380, 665 &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2361;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346;&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2325; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["19", "95", "78", "190"], "options_hi": ["19", "95", "78", "190"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>95, 380, 665</p><p></p><p>95 = 19 x 5</p><p>380 = 19 x 5 x 4</p><p>665 = 19 x 7 x 5</p><p></p><p>Therefore, the H.C.F is 19 x 5 = 95</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>95, 380, 665</p><p></p><p>95 = 19 x 5</p><p>380 = 19 x 5 x 4</p><p>665 = 19 x 7 x 5</p><p></p><p>Therefore, the H.C.F is 19 x 5 = 95</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "HCF & LCM"}, {"q_en": "<p>If (sec&#945; + tan&#945;)/(sec&#945; - tan&#945;) = 37/7, then what is the value of sin&#945;?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; (sec&#945; + tan&#945;)/(sec&#945; - tan&#945;) = 37/7, &#2340;&#2379; sin&#945; &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["22/19", "30/23", "15/22", "29/34"], "options_hi": ["22/19", "30/23", "15/22", "29/34"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>(sec&#945; + tan&#945;)/(sec&#945; - tan&#945;) = 37/7</p><p>7sec&#945; + 7tan&#945; = 37sec&#945;  -  37tan&#945;</p><p>sec&#945;/tan&#945; = 22/15</p><p>(1/cos&#945;)/(sin&#945;/cos&#945;) = 22/15</p><p>sin&#945; = 15/22</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>(sec&#945; + tan&#945;)/(sec&#945; - tan&#945;) = 37/7</p><p>7sec&#945; + 7tan&#945; = 37sec&#945;  -  37tan&#945;</p><p>sec&#945;/tan&#945; = 22/15</p><p>(1/cos&#945;)/(sin&#945;/cos&#945;) = 22/15</p><p>sin&#945; = 15/22</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Trigonometry"}, {"q_en": "<p>There are three numbers whose average is 17. Difference between largest and smallest number is 18 and the ratio of smallest to second largest number is 3 : 5. Find the sum of largest and second largest number.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2324;&#2360;&#2340; 17 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2311;&#2344;&#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2348;&#2360;&#2375; &#2348;&#2337;&#2364;&#2368; &#2324;&#2352; &#2360;&#2348;&#2360;&#2375; &#2331;&#2379;&#2335;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; 18 &#2361;&#2376; &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; &#2360;&#2348;&#2360;&#2375; &#2331;&#2379;&#2335;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2324;&#2352; &#2342;&#2370;&#2360;&#2352;&#2368; &#2360;&#2348;&#2360;&#2375; &#2348;&#2337;&#2364;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 3 : 5 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2360;&#2348;&#2360;&#2375; &#2348;&#2337;&#2364;&#2368; &#2324;&#2352; &#2342;&#2370;&#2360;&#2352;&#2368; &#2360;&#2348;&#2360;&#2375; &#2348;&#2337;&#2364;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366; &#2351;&#2379;&#2327;&#2347;&#2354; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2351;&#2375;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["48", "46", "44", "42"], "options_hi": ["48", "46", "44", "42"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Let the numbers are x, y and z in increasing order</p><p>Total of three numbers = 17 * 3 = 51</p><p>According to question,</p><p>z  -  x = 18</p><p>x : y = 3 : 5</p><p>let x and y be 3a and 5a respectively</p><p>z = 18 + x = 18 + 3a</p><p>x + y + z = 51</p><p>3a + 5a + 18 + 3a = 11a + 18</p><p>11a = 51  -  18 = 33</p><p>a = 33/11 = 3</p><p>required sum = 5a + 18 + 3a = 24 + 18 = 42</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the numbers are x, y and z in increasing order</p><p>Total of three numbers = 17 * 3 = 51</p><p>According to question,</p><p>z  -  x = 18</p><p>x : y = 3 : 5</p><p>let x and y be 3a and 5a respectively</p><p>z = 18 + x = 18 + 3a</p><p>x + y + z = 51</p><p>3a + 5a + 18 + 3a = 11a + 18</p><p>11a = 51  -  18 = 33</p><p>a = 33/11 = 3</p><p>required sum = 5a + 18 + 3a = 24 + 18 = 42</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Average"}, {"q_en": "<p>Pipes A, B, and C can fill a tank in 12 hours, 24 hours, and 16 hours respectively. If pipes A and C are opened together for one hour and pipes B and C are opened together for next one hour, and in this way the pipes are opened further for alternate hours, then find the time taken to fill the tank.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346; A, B &#2324;&#2352; C &#2319;&#2325; &#2335;&#2306;&#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 12 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;, 24 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2324;&#2352; 16 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2349;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346; A &#2324;&#2352; C &#2325;&#2379; &#2319;&#2325; &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2326;&#2379;&#2354;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; &#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346; B &#2324;&#2352; C &#2325;&#2379; &#2309;&#2327;&#2354;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2326;&#2379;&#2354;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2311;&#2360; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379; &#2319;&#2325;&#2366;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2326;&#2379;&#2354;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2335;&#2306;&#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2379; &#2349;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2354;&#2327;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2366; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["4 hours", "8 hours", "6 hours", "12 hours"], "options_hi": ["4 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;", "8 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;", "6 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;", "12 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Total capacity = L.C.M of 12, 24, and 16 = 48 unit</p><p>Efficiency = total capacity/ time taken</p><p>Efficiency of A = 48/12 = 4 unit</p><p>Efficiency of B = 48/24 = 2 unit</p><p>Efficiency of C = 48/16 = 3 unit</p><p>Required time = 2 * 48/ (7 + 5) = 8 hours</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Total capacity = L.C.M of 12, 24, and 16 = 48 unit</p><p>Efficiency = total capacity/ time taken</p><p>Efficiency of A = 48/12 = 4 unit</p><p>Efficiency of B = 48/24 = 2 unit</p><p>Efficiency of C = 48/16 = 3 unit</p><p>Required time = 2 * 48/ (7 + 5) = 8 hours</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Pipes & Cisterns"}, {"q_en": "<p>A shopkeeper wanted to sell Rs. 3000 worth of products. But he had two options, giving three successive discounts of 15% each or giving a single discount of 34%. What was the difference between the two options of discounts (in rupees)?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2342;&#2369;&#2325;&#2366;&#2344;&#2342;&#2366;&#2352; 3000 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366; &#2360;&#2366;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2344;&#2366; &#2330;&#2366;&#2361;&#2340;&#2366; &#2341;&#2366;&#2404; &#2354;&#2375;&#2325;&#2367;&#2344; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2366;&#2360; &#2342;&#2379; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2354;&#2381;&#2346; &#2341;&#2375;, 15% &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2367;&#2325; &#2331;&#2370;&#2335; &#2342;&#2375;&#2344;&#2366; &#2351;&#2366; 34% &#2325;&#2368; &#2319;&#2325; &#2331;&#2370;&#2335; &#2342;&#2375;&#2344;&#2366;&#2404; &#2331;&#2370;&#2335; &#2325;&#2375; &#2342;&#2379; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2354;&#2381;&#2346;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; (&#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2341;&#2366;?</p>", "options_en": ["Rs. 132.225", "Rs. 141.625", "Rs. 146.225", "Rs. 137.625"], "options_hi": ["&#2352;&#2369;. 132.225", "&#2352;&#2369;. 141.625", "&#2352;&#2369;. 146.225", "&#2352;&#2369;. 137.625"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Equivalent discount = 1  -  (1  -  0.15) * (1  -  0.15) * (1  -  0.15) </p><p>= 0.385875 = 38.5875% </p><p>Difference in discount = 38.5875  -  34 = 4.5875% </p><p>Hence, the required difference = 3000 * 4.5875/100 = Rs. 137.625</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Equivalent discount = 1  -  (1  -  0.15) * (1  -  0.15) * (1  -  0.15) </p><p>= 0.385875 = 38.5875% </p><p>Difference in discount = 38.5875  -  34 = 4.5875% </p><p>Hence, the required difference = 3000 * 4.5875/100 = Rs. 137.625</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Profit & Loss"}, {"q_en": "<p>Simplify:</p><p><div><div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">X(X + 8) + 4<sup>2</sup>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2379; &#2360;&#2352;&#2354;&#2368;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;:</p><p><div><div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">X(X + 8) + 4<sup>2</sup>", "options_en": ["196", "1372", "-336", "343"], "options_hi": ["196", "1372", "-336", "343"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>[X (X + 8) + 4<sup>2</sup>]/ [(X + 4)<sup>2</sup> * 1/7<sup>3</sup>]</p><p>=&gt; [X<sup>2</sup> + 8X + 16] * 343/ [(X + 4)<sup>2</sup></p><p>=&gt; [(X + 4)<sup>2</sup> * 343]/(X + 4)<sup>2</sup></p><p>=&gt; 343</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>[X (X + 8) + 4<sup>2</sup>]/ [(X + 4)<sup>2</sup> * 1/7<sup>3</sup>]</p><p>=&gt; [X<sup>2</sup> + 8X + 16] * 343/ [(X + 4)<sup>2</sup></p><p>=&gt; [(X + 4)<sup>2</sup> * 343]/(X + 4)<sup>2</sup></p><p>=&gt; 343</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simplification"}, {"q_en": "<p>The speed of Vande Bharat is 60 km/h, and it is 744 meters long, then what is the time taken by Vande Bharat to cross Rajdhani Express which is 912 meters long and running in the opposite direction at 78 km/h?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2357;&#2306;&#2342;&#2375; &#2349;&#2366;&#2352;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; 60 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2324;&#2352; &#2351;&#2361; 744 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2357;&#2306;&#2342;&#2375; &#2349;&#2366;&#2352;&#2340; &#2325;&#2379; &#2352;&#2366;&#2332;&#2343;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; &#2319;&#2325;&#2381;&#2360;&#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2360; &#2325;&#2379; &#2346;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2354;&#2327;&#2375;&#2327;&#2366; &#2332;&#2379; 912 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; 78 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; &#2360;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2346;&#2352;&#2368;&#2340; &#2342;&#2367;&#2358;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2330;&#2354; &#2352;&#2361;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["63.2 seconds", "33.2 seconds", "44.6 seconds", "43.2 seconds"], "options_hi": ["63.2 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337;", "33.2 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337;", "44.6 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337;", "43.2 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337;"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Speed of Vande Bharat = 60 km/h</p><p>And speed of Rajdhani Express = 78 km/h</p><p>Length of Vande Bharat = 744 m</p><p>And length of Rajdhani Express = 912 m</p><p>Time taken = (744 + 912)/((60 + 78) * 5/18) = 43.2 seconds</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Speed of Vande Bharat = 60 km/h</p><p>And speed of Rajdhani Express = 78 km/h</p><p>Length of Vande Bharat = 744 m</p><p>And length of Rajdhani Express = 912 m</p><p>Time taken = (744 + 912)/((60 + 78) * 5/18) = 43.2 seconds</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>Pipe A can fill a tank in 8 hours, while Pipe B can fill the same tank in 12 hours. Both pipes are opened together, and after 4 hours, the rate of Pipe B is reduced to half of its original. In how many total hours will the tank be completely filled?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346; A &#2319;&#2325; &#2335;&#2306;&#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2379; 8 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2349;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2332;&#2348;&#2325;&#2367; &#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346; B &#2313;&#2360;&#2368; &#2335;&#2306;&#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2379; 12 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2349;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2342;&#2379;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2326;&#2379;&#2354; &#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2324;&#2352; 4 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342;, &#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346; B &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2352; &#2328;&#2335;&#2325;&#2352; &#2310;&#2343;&#2368; &#2352;&#2361; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2335;&#2306;&#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; &#2340;&#2352;&#2361; &#2349;&#2352; &#2332;&#2366;&#2319;&#2327;&#2368;?</p>", "options_en": ["4", "5", "6", "7"], "options_hi": ["4", "5", "6", "7"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>A's rate = 1/8 tank per hour</p><p>B's rate = 1/12 tank per hour</p><p>Combined rate = 1/8 + 1/12 = 5/24 per hour</p><p>Work in first 4 hours = 4  X  (5/24) = 5/6 of the tank</p><p>Remaining = 1/6 of the tank</p><p>B's new rate = 1/24 per hour</p><p>New combined rate = 1/8 + 1/24 = 4/24 = 1/6 per hour</p><p>Time to finish = (1/6) &div; (1/6) = 1 hour</p><p>Total time = 4 + 1 = 5 hours</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>A's rate = 1/8 tank per hour</p><p>B's rate = 1/12 tank per hour</p><p>Combined rate = 1/8 + 1/12 = 5/24 per hour</p><p>Work in first 4 hours = 4  X  (5/24) = 5/6 of the tank</p><p>Remaining = 1/6 of the tank</p><p>B's new rate = 1/24 per hour</p><p>New combined rate = 1/8 + 1/24 = 4/24 = 1/6 per hour</p><p>Time to finish = (1/6) &div; (1/6) = 1 hour</p><p>Total time = 4 + 1 = 5 hours</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Pipes & Cisterns"}, {"q_en": "<p>What should be divided by (x<sup>2</sup> + 6x  -  5) so that the remainder is 5 and quotient is x<sup>3</sup> + 4x<sup>2</sup> + x + 15? </p>", "q_hi": "<p>(x<sup>2</sup> + 6x - 5) &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2360;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2319; &#2325;&#2367; &#2358;&#2375;&#2359;&#2347;&#2354; 5 &#2361;&#2379; &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; &#2349;&#2366;&#2327;&#2347;&#2354; x<sup>3</sup> + 4x<sup>2</sup> + x + 15 &#2361;&#2379;?</p>", "options_en": ["x<sup>5</sup> + 10x<sup>4</sup> + 20x<sup>3</sup> + x<sup>2</sup> + 85x  -  70", "x<sup>5</sup> + 12x<sup>4</sup> + 20x<sup>3</sup> + 3x<sup>2</sup> + 75x  -  80", "x<sup>5</sup> + 8x<sup>4</sup> + 10x<sup>3</sup>  -  7x<sup>2</sup> + 105x  -  70", "x<sup>5</sup> - x<sup>4</sup> + 10x<sup>3</sup> + x<sup>2</sup> + 95x  -  75"], "options_hi": ["x<sup>5</sup> + 10x<sup>4</sup> + 20x<sup>3</sup> + x<sup>2</sup> + 85x - 70", "x<sup>5</sup> + 12x<sup>4</sup> + 20x<sup>3</sup> + 3x<sup>2</sup> + 75x - 80", "x<sup>5</sup> + 8x<sup>4</sup> + 10x<sup>3</sup> - 7x<sup>2</sup> + 105x - 70", "x<sup>5</sup> - x<sup>4</sup> + 10x<sup>3</sup> + x<sup>2</sup> + 95x - 75"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Dividend = divisor * quotient + remainder</p><p>= (x<sup>2</sup> + 6x  -  5)*(x<sup>3</sup> + 4x<sup>2</sup> + x + 15) + 5</p><p>= x<sup>5</sup> + 4x<sup>4</sup> + x<sup>3</sup> + 15x<sup>2</sup> + 6x<sup>4</sup> + 24x<sup>3</sup> + 6x<sup>2</sup> + 90x  -  5x<sup>3</sup>  -  20x<sup>2</sup>  -  5x  -  75 + 5</p><p>= x<sup>5</sup> + 10x<sup>4</sup> + 20x<sup>3</sup> + x<sup>2</sup> + 85x  -  70</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Dividend = divisor * quotient + remainder</p><p>= (x<sup>2</sup> + 6x  -  5)*(x<sup>3</sup> + 4x<sup>2</sup> + x + 15) + 5</p><p>= x<sup>5</sup> + 4x<sup>4</sup> + x<sup>3</sup> + 15x<sup>2</sup> + 6x<sup>4</sup> + 24x<sup>3</sup> + 6x<sup>2</sup> + 90x  -  5x<sup>3</sup>  -  20x<sup>2</sup>  -  5x  -  75 + 5</p><p>= x<sup>5</sup> + 10x<sup>4</sup> + 20x<sup>3</sup> + x<sup>2</sup> + 85x  -  70</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Algebra"}, {"q_en": "<p>Speed of two cars M and N are 15 m/s and 40/3 m/s respectively. If car M covers a certain distance in 9 hours, then in how much time car N can cover the same distance? (correct up to two decimals)</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2342;&#2379; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; M &#2324;&#2352; N &#2325;&#2368; &#2330;&#2366;&#2354; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 15 m/s &#2324;&#2352; 40/3 m/s &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352; M &#2319;&#2325; &#2344;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2330;&#2367;&#2340; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; 9 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2340;&#2351; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352; N &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2340;&#2351; &#2325;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;? (&#2342;&#2358;&#2350;&#2354;&#2357; &#2325;&#2375; &#2342;&#2379; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2340;&#2325; &#2360;&#2361;&#2368;)</p>", "options_en": ["8.23 hours", "12.74 hours", "10.13 hours", "9.75 hours"], "options_hi": ["8.23 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;", "12.74 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;", "10.13 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;", "9.75 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>For same distance,</p><p>Speed of M/Speed of N = Time taken by N/Time taken by M</p><p>Time taken by N = [15/(40/3)] * 9 = 10.125 = 10.13 hours</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>For same distance,</p><p>Speed of M/Speed of N = Time taken by N/Time taken by M</p><p>Time taken by N = [15/(40/3)] * 9 = 10.125 = 10.13 hours</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>Simplify:</p><p>&radic;(36x<sup>2</sup> - 108x + 81)</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2360;&#2352;&#2354;&#2368;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;:</p><p>&radic;(36x<sup>2</sup> - 108x + 81)</p>", "options_en": ["6x  -  9", "2x  -  9", "5x  -  9", "3x  -  3"], "options_hi": ["6x - 9", "2x - 9", "5x - 9", "3x - 3"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p><img width=124 height=23 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20933/image067.png\"></p><p><img width=132 height=31 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20933/image068.png\"></p><p><img width=89 height=31 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20933/image069.png\"></p><p>= 3(2x  -  3)</p><p>= 6x  -  9</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=124 height=23 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20933/image067.png\"></p><p><img width=132 height=31 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20933/image068.png\"></p><p><img width=89 height=31 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20933/image069.png\"></p><p>= 3(2x  -  3)</p><p>= 6x  -  9</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simplification"}, {"q_en": "<p>The average weight of 15 students is 62 kg. If three students join the group, the average weight is increased by 500 gm, then find the average weight of three students who join the group.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>15 &#2331;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2324;&#2360;&#2340; &#2357;&#2332;&#2344; 62 kg &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2331;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352; &#2360;&#2350;&#2370;&#2361; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2358;&#2366;&#2350;&#2367;&#2354; &#2361;&#2379;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2324;&#2360;&#2340; &#2357;&#2332;&#2344; 500 gm &#2348;&#2338;&#2364; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2360;&#2350;&#2370;&#2361; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2358;&#2366;&#2350;&#2367;&#2354; &#2361;&#2379;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2331;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2324;&#2360;&#2340; &#2357;&#2332;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["63 kg", "67 kg", "64 kg", "65 kg"], "options_hi": ["63 kg", "67 kg", "64 kg", "65 kg"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>The total weight of 15 students = 15 * 62 = 930 kg</p><p>The total weight of 18 students = 18 * 62.5 = 1125 kg</p><p>The average weight of three students = (1125  -  930)/ 3 = 195/3 = 65 kg</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>The total weight of 15 students = 15 * 62 = 930 kg</p><p>The total weight of 18 students = 18 * 62.5 = 1125 kg</p><p>The average weight of three students = (1125  -  930)/ 3 = 195/3 = 65 kg</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Average"}]}